"There was a joy in the self-harming mischief\nThere was a sigh in the deserving punish'\n\nEnjoyment is inevitable and it's not at all a sin\nThere're just some healthy ways to not to have a disrespecting grin\n\nThey had some reputation\nThey were saved by it\nThey had one lifeline\nAnd it got wasted\n\nSome wept in regret\nSome had straight up acceptance\nSome had the guts to talk\nBut all were regretting and were self-gated\n\nAcceptance is not just for grief\nIt's step 1 to improve and change\nHaving guts is a different thing\nIt's good they had their punishments arranged\n\nPunishments can be good too\nThey can teach you some leasons\nNot mindlessly hurting your body\nBut letting you regain what you achieved\n\nIt was good for 'em\nThey won't repeat it again\nThey had their lessons given\nAnd they've improved in gain"